E — Employees: people live only in the store, never in files.

This folder is deliberately empty of .cosm files. E:person, E:assignment, E:membership, E:credential,
E:intake, E:continuity, E:access and E:broadcast rows are canonical in store.sqlite, built by `python -m core index` and filled by
`python -m core people import fixtures/meadow fixtures/meadow/people.yaml` (encryption at rest is phase 2). Nothing outside E may name a person; positions in O/positions.cosm are
the seats, and who holds each seat is an E:assignment in the store.

What the store will hold for Meadow (no names here, by design): one assignment per position
(chief-executive, support-lead, payroll-owner) and two for the engineer template. The Payroll Owner's
variance lives on the role in O, not on the person.

Lint rules 6, 12 and 13 (assignments, credentials, bus factor) read the store and say "store missing"
until it is built; after index and import, Meadow passes all fourteen.
